autophile@zoominternet.net writes:


> I've put up the next version of the chapter here: 
> http://www.scribd.com/doc/13404260/lojban1
> 
> I sort of side-stepped the whole stress on names issue, in the  
> interests of keeping it simple. I also re-did the names, and added  
> many more sentences.
> 
> Can anyone spot any errors?
> 

1. The capital "B" of the larger oval in footnote 1 is in a different font 
from the "B" in the text next to it.  This makes it harder to tell if they are, 
in fact, referring to the same "B".
2. ".i" is unncessary, if not wrong, after "ni'o" in the second group of 
sentences.
3. "mad'rid" is still wrong.  Apostrophes ("y'y bu") cannot come between 
consonants.  Use either "madrid" (with default stress on "ma" or "maDRID").
4. di'u "la .afrikas." is not on the map.
5. In "le remoi cipra" "bridla" should be "brivla".

General question:  Does "mo" have a place structure of its own?  IOW, is "la 
paris. mo la frans." correct?

mu'o 
mi'e stevon


